{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ConjImQPhysicalRole","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ConjImQPhysicalRole","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.not_imQPhysicalRole_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.not_imQPhysicalRole_norm","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L120-L126","doc":"Non-vacuity, negative side: the modulus `‖·‖` **does** see `Im(q)` and so\nfails the class at `q = i`. The class is therefore falsifiable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.imQPhysicalRole_realPart_nonconstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.imQPhysicalRole_realPart_nonconstant","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L114-L118","doc":"That model really is non-constant, so the positive side above is not the\ntrivial `obs = 0` witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.imQPhysicalRole_realPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.imQPhysicalRole_realPart","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L106-L112","doc":"Non-vacuity, positive side: taking the real part is a **non-constant**\nobservable satisfying the class at every `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.im_q_undetermined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.im_q_undetermined","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L95-L104","doc":"**Payoff.** An observable satisfying the class cannot tell the substrate\nmodulus `q` from a *real* number: some point with zero imaginary part,\ndistinct from `q`, carries the same observable value. This is the precise\nsense in which `Im(q)` has no current observable. The conclusion is not a\nclass field — it is derived from `leading_order_real`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.obs_conj_invariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.obs_conj_invariance","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L87-L93","doc":"Derived from the first field alone: a modulus observable is blind to the\n**sign** of `Im(q)`. Weaker than the conjecture — see the scope note. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ImQPhysicalRole.leading_order_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ImQPhysicalRole.leading_order_real","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L83-L83","doc":"At leading order the observable does not move when `Im(q)` is discarded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ImQPhysicalRole.factors_through_modulus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ImQPhysicalRole.factors_through_modulus","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The observable is the modulus of a conjugation-equivariant map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ImQPhysicalRole.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ImQPhysicalRole.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ImQPhysicalRole","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ImQPhysicalRole","kind":"class","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L68-L83","doc":"**Conjecture (primary, §3b-tax).** The real observable `obs` cannot resolve\n`Im(q)` at the substrate modulus `q`: it factors through the modulus of a\nconjugation-equivariant map, and at leading order its value at `q` agrees\nwith its value at `Re q`.\n\nBoth fields are hypotheses about the *observable*, not about `Im(q)`; the\nconclusion that `Im(q)` is undetermined is derived below. There is\ndeliberately **no instance** for the QOU mass observable — supplying one is\nthe open work. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:im-q-physical-role","label":"conj:im-q-physical-role","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ImQCandidateRole.non_hermitian_deformation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ImQCandidateRole.non_hermitian_deformation","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ImQCandidateRole.phase_dual_to_cal2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ImQCandidateRole.phase_dual_to_cal2","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ImQCandidateRole.chirality_orientation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ImQCandidateRole.chirality_orientation","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ImQCandidateRole","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ImQCandidateRole","kind":"inductive","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L61-L66","doc":"Three candidate roles for `Im(q)`, enumerated for audit visibility. The\nconjecture does not pick one; identifying the physical role is open work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.mass_observable_conj_invariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.mass_observable_conj_invariance","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L49-L59","doc":"Under modulus projection (categorical mass formula), a mass observable\n`m(q) = |F(q)|` is invariant under `q ↦ q̄` for any conjugation-equivariant\n`F` — in particular for a real-coefficient polynomial (e.g. the Markov\ntrace), where `F(q̄) = F(q)‾` holds and is supplied as the hypothesis `hF`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.default_q_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.default_q_real","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-im-q-physical-role.lean#L46-L47","doc":"The default substrate convention sets `Im(q) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}